  "notes": "Modified cash basis city (recorded as cash basis). Governmental lines from the Governmental Funds Statement of Receipts, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p5, Total Governmental Funds column); Golf, Housing, CDBG and Street are governmental funds. beginning_cash/ending_cash are the modified-cash fund balances the statement rolls forward (1,126,073 / 601,215); they include Due from Stanton Nursing Home 61,755 and notes receivable offset by deferred revenues (p4). Transfers are printed net per fund; transfers_in/out are the positive/negative fund columns (net (327,729) to the Utilities Fund). Business-type lines from the Proprietary Fund Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p7, Utilities Fund, accrual items incl. depreciation): measure net position 1,395,368 -> 1,803,774; the government-wide statements (p1-3) show the business-type activities on a cash basis (80,415). The proprietary cash flow statement (p8) is not recorded (proprietary is for GAAP reports). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p4, totals equal the government-wide figures), business-type lines and totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (p9), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds and proprietary fund statements; the Utilities Fund has no printed revenue total (operating 463,955 + interest 9,391). 'Other Taxes' 417,929 has no printed breakdown by tax type. Governmental identity: 1,126,073 + 1,714,209 - 1,911,338 + 321,021 - 648,750 = 601,215. Business identity: 1,395,368 + 473,346 - 392,669 + 327,729 = 1,803,774. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
